(639093, 66384, 14043, '<td valign="top">Good use of DOF.  However, this is clearly not orange as at the front of the car there is a painted on light which is orange whereas the rest of the car is red.  Score: 4</td>', 'Good use of DOF.  However, this is clearly not orange as at the front of the car there is a painted on light which is orange whereas the rest of the car is red.  Score: 4', '2004-03-25 23:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(639098, 65560, 14043, '<td valign="top">Blurry, bad reflections on the silverware.  The whole spoon should be in the shot as well as the fork, or crop the fork closer to match the knife.  The different lighting on the knife and fork is distracting.  Score: 3</td>', 'Blurry, bad reflections on the silverware.  The whole spoon should be in the shot as well as the fork, or crop the fork closer to match the knife.  The different lighting on the knife and fork is distracting.  Score: 3', '2004-03-25 23:26:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(639101, 66149, 14043, '<td valign="top">Very, very red.  I''m assuming you noticed this because you included "love" in your title and I have never seen that used in conjunction with orange before.  I like the use of the black on red though and the combination works well.  However the reflection on the glass is distracting.  Score: 4</td>', 'Very, very red.  I''m assuming you noticed this because you included "love" in your title and I have never seen that used in conjunction with orange before.  I like the use of the black on red though and the combination works well.  However the reflection on the glass is distracting.  Score: 4', '2004-03-25 23:28:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(639105, 66212, 14043, '<td valign="top">Erm...Nice idea, but too staged looking for not being in a studio.  Perhaps try actually dropping them and see how they land.  The overcompression of your file made it a bit blurry.  I do like the off-set and not just centering the can.  Perhaps boost the contrast to make everything brighter and make the wall whiter.  Score: 3</td>', 'Erm...Nice idea, but too staged looking for not being in a studio.  Perhaps try actually dropping them and see how they land.  The overcompression of your file made it a bit blurry.  I do like the off-set and not just centering the can.  Perhaps boost the contrast to make everything brighter and make the wall whiter.  Score: 3', '2004-03-25 23:32:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(639107, 65967, 14043, '<td valign="top">Turning it into a "negative" is not taking an interesting picture.  Yes, there is a lot of orange, but it was no in the original.  Try cropping more on the left to cut off the lonely spire edge and then add more of the tree to the right of the hotel.  Score: 3</td>', 'Turning it into a "negative" is not taking an interesting picture.  Yes, there is a lot of orange, but it was no in the original.  Try cropping more on the left to cut off the lonely spire edge and then add more of the tree to the right of the hotel.  Score: 3', '2004-03-25 23:34:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(639113, 65619, 14043, '<td valign="top">Purple, Yellow, Red.  Orange?  Try cropping to cut off the purple ones and the end of the poll to the right.  Up the contrast to make the white wall, white and rotate to level out the pole they are hanging on.  Score: 3<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-31 01:26:33.</i></td>', 'Purple, Yellow, Red.  Orange?  Try cropping to cut off the purple ones and the end of the poll to the right.  Up the contrast to make the white wall, white and rotate to level out the pole they are hanging on.  Score: 3', '2004-03-25 23:36:37.000000', '2004-03-31 02:26:33.000000', 1),
