(644669, 66429, 12253, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work!  I am shocked this did not ribbon.  I am also shocked at the number of 1s, 2s, and 3s.  Come on people! <br/> <br/>Anyway, congrats on a great finish.</td>', 'Beautiful work!  I am shocked this did not ribbon.  I am also shocked at the number of 1s, 2s, and 3s.  Come on people!  Anyway, congrats on a great finish.', '2004-03-31 01:04:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(644673, 65993, 16106, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rasai:</b></div><hr/><i> Yep, THe HOTTEST March ever here in the city .... but it wasn''t that HOT! The more I look at this the more I wonder? You are up above the water quite a bit in this picture... Was this taken with a SUPER Telephoto, or perhaps in a low flying aircraft?  My only other guess would be at the top of a VERY TALL ship? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> Ya, quite a ways away. I used a 500 mm lens to shoot in the parking lot of lawrence hall of science in the berkeley hills.<br/> After I submited I realised that I sharpened once too often and got the ghosting on the suspension supports, live and learn.<br/> Thanks for all the kind words and fine crits.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-31 00:09:43.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Rasai: Yep, THe HOTTEST March ever here in the city .... but it wasn''t that HOT! The more I look at this the more I wonder? You are up above the water quite a bit in this picture... Was this taken with a SUPER Telephoto, or perhaps in a low flying aircraft?  My only other guess would be at the top of a VERY TALL ship?   Ya, quite a ways away. I used a 500 mm lens to shoot in the parking lot of lawrence hall of science in the berkeley hills. After I submited I realised that I sharpened once too often and got the ghosting on the suspension supports, live and learn. Thanks for all the kind words and fine crits.', '2004-03-31 01:07:14.000000', '2004-03-31 01:09:43.000000', 0),
(644674, 65272, 5318, '<td valign="top">Wow, wonderful movement. Love that dress!Great job!  11th  WOOHOO!!!!</td>', 'Wow, wonderful movement. Love that dress!Great job!  11th  WOOHOO!!!!', '2004-03-31 01:07:21.000000', NULL, 0),
