(645184, 66399, 4041, '<td valign="top">yeah, i had to bake the crayon first to soften it enough to be able to carve.  i think i went through a dozen other colors practicing.  it was late on the submission night and i was havin a helluva time trying to get them A) the right size and B) keeping them together.  had i thought of this earlier i prob would have put more than a couple of hours into it.....  thanks for the insight</td>', 'yeah, i had to bake the crayon first to soften it enough to be able to carve.  i think i went through a dozen other colors practicing.  it was late on the submission night and i was havin a helluva time trying to get them A) the right size and B) keeping them together.  had i thought of this earlier i prob would have put more than a couple of hours into it.....  thanks for the insight', '2004-03-31 09:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(645190, 66069, 472, '<td valign="top">gorgeous :) .. congrats</td>', 'gorgeous :) .. congrats', '2004-03-31 09:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(645230, 66193, 17505, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I think people were very generous with their votes on this shot. Once I entered it I was very unhappy with it. I''d set up a workbench and tools still life with an orange cord and light and soon got caried away with the shapes of the plastic on the light rather than the photo as a whole. I agree that it''s sort of empty. Thanks for the ''high'' marks anyway.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I think people were very generous with their votes on this shot. Once I entered it I was very unhappy with it. I''d set up a workbench and tools still life with an orange cord and light and soon got caried away with the shapes of the plastic on the light rather than the photo as a whole. I agree that it''s sort of empty. Thanks for the ''high'' marks anyway.', '2004-03-31 09:45:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(645234, 65383, 10634, '<td valign="top">Not out of focus. What you see is the reflection of the element in the shiny oven interior. Since spot editing is not allowed, I had to crop out as much as possible and take my chances. The two bumps of orange on the left of the element are where the "foot" is. Thanks for the comments anyway. I did use a tripod (with the 3800 you have to if you are not using the flash) and I doubt that the oven moved. :-)</td>', 'Not out of focus. What you see is the reflection of the element in the shiny oven interior. Since spot editing is not allowed, I had to crop out as much as possible and take my chances. The two bumps of orange on the left of the element are where the "foot" is. Thanks for the comments anyway. I did use a tripod (with the 3800 you have to if you are not using the flash) and I doubt that the oven moved. :-)', '2004-03-31 09:48:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(645274, 65220, 17446, '<td valign="top">thank you all for your comments.</td>', 'thank you all for your comments.', '2004-03-31 10:07:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(645295, 66069, 18709, '<td valign="top">Good choice for the winner.  I didn''t see a better shot.</td>', 'Good choice for the winner.  I didn''t see a better shot.', '2004-03-31 10:16:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(645325, 65458, 2464, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for the comments very much appreciated. Good learning experience for me. Considered that I''m really new to photography, all the comments from the Title to the Post editing has helped.<br/> <br/>To Sammie this was taken in Singapore, my country of residence, basically most of the landed property here in Singapore look very much like that.<br/> <br/>The title was a last minute attempt as I had submitted this really at the last minute and pretty much just cropped the photo and sent it in on the dateline. I do agree after looking at the shot, could have come up with something better. :)<br/> <br/>Josevillacorte, I would love to view the shots please e-mail me when you''ve posted them.<br/> <br/>Hopefully I''d do better the next round. Thanks to all and keep those comments coming in.<br/></td>', 'Thank you everyone for the comments very much appreciated. Good learning experience for me. Considered that I''m really new to photography, all the comments from the Title to the Post editing has helped. To Sammie this was taken in Singapore, my country of residence, basically most of the landed property here in Singapore look very much like that. The title was a last minute attempt as I had submitted this really at the last minute and pretty much just cropped the photo and sent it in on the dateline. I do agree after looking at the shot, could have come up with something better. :) Josevillacorte, I would love to view the shots please e-mail me when you''ve posted them. Hopefully I''d do better the next round. Thanks to all and keep those comments coming in.', '2004-03-31 10:30:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(645336, 65272, 714, '<td valign="top">Thanks Jason and Calvus.  <br/> <br/>Some of you thought I took some color out.  I did NOT take any color out.  This is what Wyoming looks like this time of year. :-) We don''t get spring till the end of April.<br/> <br/>Thanks all for the comments.  I know you spent alot of time on that.  Keep them coming.</td>', 'Thanks Jason and Calvus.   Some of you thought I took some color out.  I did NOT take any color out.  This is what Wyoming looks like this time of year. :-) We don''t get spring till the end of April. Thanks all for the comments.  I know you spent alot of time on that.  Keep them coming.', '2004-03-31 10:33:24.000000', NULL, 0),
