(645523, 65256, 18419, '<td valign="top">I''d just like to thank Mssrs. Budweiser and Coors for fueling the inspiration and willingness to submit this picture for consideration.<br/>&lt;sigh&gt; The main problem, as LtHousLady pointed out, was that the clothes hanger supporting the carrot was too springy and I couldn''t get the dumb thing to remain still.  Plus, the graph on the monitor should''ve been another color, as it was kind of taking away the orange focus.<br/>The irony is that the book in the back left was on digital photography!<br/>Thanks everyone!<br/>Stu<br/></td>', 'I''d just like to thank Mssrs. Budweiser and Coors for fueling the inspiration and willingness to submit this picture for consideration.<sigh> The main problem, as LtHousLady pointed out, was that the clothes hanger supporting the carrot was too springy and I couldn''t get the dumb thing to remain still.  Plus, the graph on the monitor should''ve been another color, as it was kind of taking away the orange focus.The irony is that the book in the back left was on digital photography!Thanks everyone!Stu', '2004-03-31 11:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(645526, 66368, 1712, '<td valign="top">This shot was a orange Carnation! I just stuck it in soft focus and sharpened it a bit! I would like to hear some more ways I could have made it better! I for one would not give a one! My lowest was probably 3 on photos! Except for bad photos I give ones!<br/> <br/>Thank you for the comments!</td>', 'This shot was a orange Carnation! I just stuck it in soft focus and sharpened it a bit! I would like to hear some more ways I could have made it better! I for one would not give a one! My lowest was probably 3 on photos! Except for bad photos I give ones! Thank you for the comments!', '2004-03-31 11:35:24.000000', NULL, 0),
