(652647, 65631, 6130, '<td valign="top">So beautiful.(not ugly)</td>', 'So beautiful.(not ugly)', '2004-04-04 09:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(654391, 65383, 8860, '<td valign="top">Whether out of focus or not - the perception by many is that it is! It''s quite useful to note the negatives since, without a description to accompany the shot, you may not be conveying your concept as desired by photography alone.<br/> <br/>For what it''s worth I think the composition is quite poor leaving much too much black at the top and with no real detail to latch on to. It is orange but that is not enough to make a good shot stand alone outside of the challenge.</td>', 'Whether out of focus or not - the perception by many is that it is! It''s quite useful to note the negatives since, without a description to accompany the shot, you may not be conveying your concept as desired by photography alone. For what it''s worth I think the composition is quite poor leaving much too much black at the top and with no real detail to latch on to. It is orange but that is not enough to make a good shot stand alone outside of the challenge.', '2004-04-05 14:24:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(654403, 66229, 10635, '<td valign="top">I was pleased with the way this turned out.  I placed a table on the window sill, with another table on top of that, then I placed the glass at the edge of the top table and set the tripod at shoulder height on the ground.  I think the angle of the camera to glass is what gave it the mirrored effect in the glass and liquid. I was also lucky, as the sky was clouded, with no blue areas.  The sun was just lighting up the edges which is what gives this a nice illuminated look.</td>', 'I was pleased with the way this turned out.  I placed a table on the window sill, with another table on top of that, then I placed the glass at the edge of the top table and set the tripod at shoulder height on the ground.  I think the angle of the camera to glass is what gave it the mirrored effect in the glass and liquid. I was also lucky, as the sky was clouded, with no blue areas.  The sun was just lighting up the edges which is what gives this a nice illuminated look.', '2004-04-05 14:35:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(654927, 65982, 14614, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who took the time to comment and vote.  I''m sorry I didn''t do this beauty justice in my photo.  That''s real close to the color of the car I found parked on a side street in Charleston SC.  Not mine &lt;she sighs&gt;.  Well cared for except for the poop (as bestagent so astutely noticed) that I wish I could have cloned out.  About all I did was crop the shot to omit distracting background stuff.  <br/> <br/>LisaAus: I tried to get my husband to break into the car, sit in the back seat and wave but, oddly, he refused!</td>', 'Thanks to all who took the time to comment and vote.  I''m sorry I didn''t do this beauty justice in my photo.  That''s real close to the color of the car I found parked on a side street in Charleston SC.  Not mine <she sighs>.  Well cared for except for the poop (as bestagent so astutely noticed) that I wish I could have cloned out.  About all I did was crop the shot to omit distracting background stuff.   LisaAus: I tried to get my husband to break into the car, sit in the back seat and wave but, oddly, he refused!', '2004-04-05 22:37:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(654966, 65531, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi Sfalice...<br/> <br/>I think you succeeded in creating ''orange'' where none existed.  Unfortunately, I think your subject suffered from the process.  The detail and interest in this flower is in the shapes and textures of the bloom.  Your back lighting makes the background more of the subject than the flower itself.  Unfortunately, there is probably no way to correct this with your choice of subject.  When I see a photo like this, I normally believe that the challenge topic is all the photographer had in mind.  Sometimes a photo suffers when something is ''forced'' into the challenge when it normally doesn''t belong.  In my humble opinion, I would have saved the marigold for a personal photograph and searched for something better fitting in the challenge.<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi Sfalice... I think you succeeded in creating ''orange'' where none existed.  Unfortunately, I think your subject suffered from the process.  The detail and interest in this flower is in the shapes and textures of the bloom.  Your back lighting makes the background more of the subject than the flower itself.  Unfortunately, there is probably no way to correct this with your choice of subject.  When I see a photo like this, I normally believe that the challenge topic is all the photographer had in mind.  Sometimes a photo suffers when something is ''forced'' into the challenge when it normally doesn''t belong.  In my humble opinion, I would have saved the marigold for a personal photograph and searched for something better fitting in the challenge. John Setzler', '2004-04-05 23:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(654970, 65128, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi Vtruan :)<br/> <br/>This is a phenomenal photograph.  I gave it a 10.  Unfortunately, you probably suffered from the ''not enough orange in my face'' syndrome in the challenge.  The detail, tone, and overall aesthetics of this photo are just great.  <br/> <br/>Great work as usual :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi Vtruan :) This is a phenomenal photograph.  I gave it a 10.  Unfortunately, you probably suffered from the ''not enough orange in my face'' syndrome in the challenge.  The detail, tone, and overall aesthetics of this photo are just great.   Great work as usual :) John Setzler ', '2004-04-05 23:32:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(654990, 65128, 3569, '<td valign="top">Thanks John for the critique &amp; 10. I appriciate all the comments from all you folks.  It was a fun shot, as soon as my daughter brought the crayfish to me it said "orange" It was quite dead, winter kill I assume.  I just set it on a wooden fishing pier and started shooting it at different angles in natural sunlight. Van</td>', 'Thanks John for the critique & 10. I appriciate all the comments from all you folks.  It was a fun shot, as soon as my daughter brought the crayfish to me it said "orange" It was quite dead, winter kill I assume.  I just set it on a wooden fishing pier and started shooting it at different angles in natural sunlight. Van', '2004-04-05 23:58:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(655251, 65993, 19569, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  Beautiful shot.</td>', 'Congratulations!  Beautiful shot.', '2004-04-06 09:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(655403, 65175, 12962, '<td valign="top">Not sure why you got ones, but the focus on the boy is wonderful - even with the busyness, my eyes go to the boy first then look around.</td>', 'Not sure why you got ones, but the focus on the boy is wonderful - even with the busyness, my eyes go to the boy first then look around.', '2004-04-06 12:05:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(655633, 65983, 9763, '<td valign="top">I would love to know what this is a photo of?  I love it!  I just have no idea what this is or how it was taken...</td>', 'I would love to know what this is a photo of?  I love it!  I just have no idea what this is or how it was taken...', '2004-04-06 14:35:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(655954, 66095, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi Eostyles...<br/> <br/>This is a nice product shot.. very well executed.  I haven''t read your comments yet but I have no Idea why this didn''t score much better than it did.  Maybe when I read those comments, it will reveal a secret :)<br/> <br/>Maybe the image, even though well executed, doesn''t ''touch'' anyone.  Product photography often has this effect.  It doesn''t speak to me in any way other than to make me ask myself "would I buy a pair of these glasses?"  <br/> <br/>It appears that your border and your composition are in question from the comments... The composition is fine, in my opinion.  The border may be a bit overdone, but it''s not a point loss from me...<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi Eostyles... This is a nice product shot.. very well executed.  I haven''t read your comments yet but I have no Idea why this didn''t score much better than it did.  Maybe when I read those comments, it will reveal a secret :) Maybe the image, even though well executed, doesn''t ''touch'' anyone.  Product photography often has this effect.  It doesn''t speak to me in any way other than to make me ask myself "would I buy a pair of these glasses?"   It appears that your border and your composition are in question from the comments... The composition is fine, in my opinion.  The border may be a bit overdone, but it''s not a point loss from me... John Setzler', '2004-04-06 20:29:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(655956, 66435, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Gracious...<br/> <br/>Nice sunset shot.  The sky is beautiful :)<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I think this photo is a bit lacking.  I like landscapes that have an ''entry path''.  This photo feels to me like it lacks grounding... a place for me to stand as I view the shot.  Maybe you can find a composition that creates a nice foreground in this scene.  Create that ''footing'' and create a pathway.... <br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Gracious... Nice sunset shot.  The sky is beautiful :) Compositionally, I think this photo is a bit lacking.  I like landscapes that have an ''entry path''.  This photo feels to me like it lacks grounding... a place for me to stand as I view the shot.  Maybe you can find a composition that creates a nice foreground in this scene.  Create that ''footing'' and create a pathway....  Keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2004-04-06 20:34:25.000000', NULL, 0),
